# Macavation — Cursor rules

Project-specific AI rules live in **`.cursor/rules/`** (for example `user-guide-update.mdc`, `user-guide-on-webportal-changes.mdc`, `no-e2e-test-results-in-git.mdc`, **`supabase-dev-uat.mdc`** on the dev branch).

The Web Portal app is under **`WebPortal/`**. Database changes belong in **`migrations/`**. E2E tests and help screenshot capture: **`Playwright Tests/`** (see `Playwright Tests/README.md`).

Legacy notes and one-off guides: **`docs/markdown-archive/`**.

## Supabase — dev branch → UAT (never FruitLive)

On the **`dev`** branch, use the **Macavation UAT** Supabase project (`nmdmddugxclpqrwylyfa`). **Never** run migrations, SQL, seeds, or MCP database work against **FruitLive** (`iwxmuemrfopajwvqdiae`) unless explicitly requested.

- **Apply migrations:** `npm run db:apply -- migrations/….sql` (CLI linked to `nmdmddugxclpqrwylyfa` per `supabase/remote.toml`)
- **Before MCP DB tools:** call `get_project_url` — must be `https://nmdmddugxclpqrwylyfa.supabase.co`
- **Portal anon key:** set `uat.anonKey` in `supabase/projects.json`, then `npm run supabase:sync-portal`
- **Guardrail:** `npm run db:check-project`

Full workflow: [`.cursor/rules/supabase-dev-uat.mdc`](.cursor/rules/supabase-dev-uat.mdc) · [UAT setup](docs/setup/UAT_DATABASE.md)
